# Input trust

Treat all external input as untrusted: HTTP bodies, query parameters, headers, cookies, webhooks, CLI arguments, file uploads, and third-party tool output.

Use parameterized queries or prepared statements. Never concatenate user input into SQL or shell commands.

Validate and encode output for its context (HTML, JSON, logs). Do not pass unsanitized input to `eval`, `exec`, dynamic SQL, or shell interpolation.

When input provenance is unclear, verify before acting on it.
